 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Near the front so people can see it and park near the entrance. Then spot the white pole for pitching the tent pegs. Perfect. Campsites hate tents under trees, they say it for safety. In practice it' about shade. Walk around it. Trees usually have weaker arm that you can cut off level with the others. Fire is for heating and cooking, lighting, and safety. Tent pitching is for tents to do. Move on. The tree is yours. And you can always ask the staff to help you find spot. They' love you for it.",
